{% comment %}
    Finding status toggle: three radios rendered as library choice tiles
    (Satisfied / Not Satisfied / N/A). Visual state is driven by
    `buttonState(finding)` so the `_pendingNA` rule lives in exactly one
    place; do not re-derive it in this template. The tiles bind the real
    control through x_name / x_checked / x_disabled / x_click, because the
    answer only exists in the browser. The pending-NA intermediate paints
    through --choice-accent, the component's documented override path.
    Used inside an x-for loop with `finding` variable in scope.
{% endcomment %}
<c-layout.choice-group class="shrink-0" aria-label="Finding status">
<c-layout.choice value="satisfied" accent="success" icon="fas fa-check" x_name="'finding-status-' + finding.finding_id" x_checked="buttonState(finding) === 'satisfied'" x_click="setFindingStatus(finding, 'satisfied')">Satisfied</c-layout.choice>
<c-layout.choice value="not-satisfied" accent="danger" icon="fas fa-times" x_name="'finding-status-' + finding.finding_id" x_checked="buttonState(finding) === 'not-satisfied'" x_click="setFindingStatus(finding, 'not-satisfied')">Not Satisfied</c-layout.choice>
<c-layout.choice value="not-applicable" accent="secondary" x_name="'finding-status-' + finding.finding_id" x_checked="buttonState(finding) === 'not-applicable' || buttonState(finding) === 'pending-na'" x_disabled="finding.is_mandatory" x_click="setFindingStatus(finding, 'not-applicable')" ::style="buttonState(finding) === 'pending-na' ? '--choice-accent: var(--color-warning)' : ''" ::title="finding.is_mandatory ? 'Part II controls are always mandatory (CRA Art 13(4))' : buttonState(finding) === 'pending-na' ? 'Awaiting justification: provide one to commit N/A' : 'Mark as not applicable'">N/A</c-layout.choice>
</c-layout.choice-group>
